# SA2A conformance -- graph-global falsifier (N3 denial rule).
#
# graphlaw parses `{ BODY } => false .` into a denial rule
# (praxis-graphlaw src/parser/n3.pest:302-303 `DenyHead = { "false" }`,
#  src/rule.rs:45 DENIAL_HEAD_MARKER). `TripleStore::check_denials/0`
# (src/lib.rs:407) queries every denial body and reports one
# `DENIED: {...} => false.` string per body that has ANY binding. The wasm's
# validate_all surfaces this as the N3_DENIAL dialect: ADMITTED when the
# violation list is empty, REFUSED otherwise.
#
# This is a GRAPH-GLOBAL constraint, not a per-node shape: no SHACL shape or
# ShEx triple constraint expresses "no agent anywhere may be simultaneously
# admitted and revoked", because the falsifier is about the co-occurrence of
# two independent memberships rather than about one focus node's properties.
#
# base.ttl asserts no ex:Revoked, so this denial is NOT tripped by the base
# graph. negative/falsifier_positive.ttl trips it.

@prefix ex: <http://example.org/sa2a/> .

{ ?a a ex:Agent . ?a a ex:Revoked } => false .
